<h1>PathoAI - Clinical AI Decision-Support System</h1>
<p class="sub">Nodal Metastasis Risk Prediction using Multi-Instance Learning (MIL)<br>Project Technology Overview Document</p>
<div class="box"><strong>Document Purpose:</strong> This document provides a comprehensive overview of the PathoAI project - its purpose, system architecture, and all technologies used across the frontend, backend, AI inference service, and database layers.</div>
<hr>
<h2>1. Project Overview</h2>
<p>PathoAI is a production-structured, end-to-end <strong>clinical AI decision-support web application</strong> designed to predict the risk of <strong>Nodal Metastasis</strong> from Biopsy Histology Images using <strong>Multi-Instance Learning (MIL)</strong>.</p>
<p>The system assists pathologists and oncologists by analyzing digitized biopsy slide images and generating a risk classification (<strong>LOW</strong>, <strong>MODERATE</strong>, or <strong>HIGH</strong>) for nodal metastasis, supporting clinical decision-making without replacing physician judgment.</p>
<p>The application follows a <strong>monorepo microservices architecture</strong> with three independently runnable services: a React frontend, a Node.js/Express backend, and a Python FastAPI AI inference service.</p>
<hr>
<h2>2. System Architecture</h2>
<p>The system is organized as three loosely coupled tiers communicating over HTTP:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Frontend (React + Vite)</strong> - Clinical user interface for doctors to manage patients, upload biopsy slides, and view AI risk reports.</li>
<li><strong>Backend REST API (Node.js + Express)</strong> - Handles authentication, patient management, image uploads, and orchestrates AI inference requests.</li>
<li><strong>AI Inference Service (Python + FastAPI)</strong> - Accepts biopsy images, runs MIL inference, and returns risk scores and attention maps.</li>
</ul>
<table>
<tr><th>Service</th><th>Technology</th><th>Port</th><th>Local URL</th></tr>
<tr><td>Frontend Web App</td><td>React 18 + Vite</td><td>80</td><td>http://localhost</td></tr>
<tr><td>Backend REST API</td><td>Node.js + Express + TypeScript</td><td>5000</td><td>http://localhost:5000</td></tr>
<tr><td>AI Inference Service</td><td>Python + FastAPI + MIL</td><td>8000</td><td>http://localhost:8000</td></tr>
</table>
<hr>
<h2>3. Technologies Used</h2>
<h3>3.1 Frontend Technologies</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Technology</th><th>Version</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
