</table>
<h3>3.4 Database and Storage</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Technology</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td>Supabase</td><td>Backend-as-a-Service with hosted PostgreSQL and file storage</td></tr>
<tr><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>Relational database for doctors, patients, predictions, and biopsy images</td></tr>
<tr><td>In-Memory Store (Fallback)</td><td>Local dev fallback with pre-seeded demo data when Supabase is unavailable</td></tr>
</table>
<h3>3.5 Developer Tools and DevOps</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Tool</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
<tr><td>npm Monorepo</td><td>Single root project managing all three services with shared scripts</td></tr>
<tr><td>Concurrently</td><td>Runs all services simultaneously with one command: npm run dev</td></tr>
<tr><td>ESLint</td><td>JavaScript and TypeScript code linting</td></tr>
<tr><td>Git</td><td>Version control and source management</td></tr>
</table>
<hr>
<h2>4. Key Features</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Doctor Authentication and Role Scoping</strong> - JWT-based secure login, bcrypt password hashing, and complete profile management.</li>
<li><strong>Patient Clinical Registry</strong> - Searchable, filterable, sortable and paginated medical records.</li>
<li><strong>13-Step Prediction Workflow</strong> - Patient selection, biopsy slide upload (JPEG, PNG, TIFF, WebP, SVS), file validation, processing, risk score, and printable report.</li>
<li><strong>Risk Classification</strong> - LOW / MODERATE / HIGH nodal metastasis risk with probability and confidence scores.</li>
<li><strong>Dual Inference Mode</strong> - Demo mode (deterministic simulation) and Real mode (Python MIL microservice).</li>
<li><strong>Printable Clinical Reports</strong> - PDF-ready reports with mandatory clinical disclaimers.</li>
<li><strong>In-Memory Fallback Database</strong> - Works offline with pre-seeded demo account.</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h2>5. AI Model - Multi-Instance Learning (MIL)</h2>
<p>The AI backbone uses <strong>Multi-Instance Learning (MIL)</strong>, specifically the <strong>CLAM (Clustering-constrained Attention MIL)</strong> architecture.</p>
<ul>
<li>Whole-slide biopsy images are too large for single-pass inference (often gigapixels).</li>
<li>MIL treats the slide as a <strong>bag</strong> of smaller image patches (instances).</li>
<li>An <strong>attention mechanism</strong> weights the most diagnostically relevant patches.</li>
<li>Bag-level prediction aggregates all patch-level features into a single risk score.</li>
</ul>
<p>Outputs: prediction result, risk category, probability score, confidence score, and bag statistics (total patches, high-attention patches, top feature score).</p>
<hr>
<h2>6. Prerequisites to Run the Project</h2>
<ul>
<li>Node.js 18+ and npm 9+</li>
<li>Python 3.10+ with pip</li>
<li>Supabase account (optional - falls back to in-memory if not configured)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Install all dependencies:</strong></p>
<p style="font-family: Courier New, monospace; background-color: #f4f4f4; padding: 8pt;">npm run install:all</p>
<p><strong>Start all services:</strong></p>
<p style="font-family: Courier New, monospace; background-color: #f4f4f4; padding: 8pt;">npm run dev</p>
<hr>
